      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T02:52:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, I expect %s to format the same way as String(), since that\u0027s what it does if there\u0027s no Format function. Admittedly the same can be said for %v, but its description to use \"a default format\" I think gives more leeway for ad-hoc special behaviour than %s\u0027s \"the uninterpreted bytes of the string\".\n\nIn any case I can\u0027t find much guidance from Go resources on how custom formatters ought to behave. Do you have a source?\n\nThe reason I added this was mainly for debug logging convenience; I use %v to show me any object in some hopefully helpful form. The reason for supporting %s is mostly compatibility - I think it\u0027s more likely existing code may use %s to get an implicit call to String(), rather than relying on %v for that.",
      "parentUuid": "b7a3b56f_5b1a2ddd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 341,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 343,
        "endChar": 14
