      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T22:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know of any explicit guidance, but https://golang.org/doc/effective_go#printing says \"If you just want the default conversion, such as decimal for integers, you can use the catchall format %v (for “value”); the result is exactly what Print and Println would produce.\".  Print is going to use Stringer, not Format(.., \u0027v).\n\nI usually view %v as a shortcut for not having to know which verb goes with your type.  If you don\u0027t want to make %s the same as %v I\u0027d suggest leaving both as-is and calling a different method manually if you want to print something more detailed.",
      "parentUuid": "0ec1af90_c08f8ae1",
      "range": {
